messages:
tori: opened PR 4233 for a migration note: onprem-installer v1 -> v2 (HSM plugin changes + network rules). Need doc review and an SDK snippet for PKCS11 users. PTAL @jamal @priya
jamal: Thanks. Two immediate asks: 1) include a short Go SDK example showing PKCS11 init + slot selection. 2) clarify that v2 renames PKCS11 env to PKCS11_LIB_PATH_V2 (backwards compatible but prefer new var).
priya: Good catch on the env var. Suggest wording: "Installer supports PKCS11_LIB_PATH (legacy) and PKCS11_LIB_PATH_V2 (preferred). If both set, V2 takes precedence."
jamal: Go snippet (very small):
```go
import (
 "github.com/miekg/pkcs11"
)
// open lib
p := pkcs11.New(os.Getenv("PKCS11_LIB_PATH_V2"))
err := p.Initialize()
// find first token with label "redwood"
slots, _ := p.GetSlotList(true)
for _, s := range slots {
  info, _ := p.GetTokenInfo(s)
  if strings.Contains(info.Label, "REDWOOD") {
    // use slot s
  }
}
```
priya: Please make the snippet tiny and link to upstream pkcs11 lib. Also add a note about mapping device nodes into container runtimes and rootless podman caveat.
security: Add a brief blurb: DO NOT commit PKCS11 paths or certs to repo. Recommend using KMS proxy with mTLS for sealed sites; provide cert rotation tip (short command to generate CSR).
tori: I'll add KMS proxy example: `kms-socket-proxy --listen 127.0.0.1:8443 --backend unix:/var/run/pkcs11.sock --tls-cert /etc/kms/proxy.crt --tls-key /etc/kms/proxy.key` and mention using a CA-signed cert for prod.
jamal: Also include nftables->iptables conversion note for customers on legacy boxes. Example iptables fallback: `iptables -A FORWARD -p tcp --dport 443 -j ACCEPT; iptables -A FORWARD -p tcp --dport 22 -j ACCEPT; iptables -A FORWARD -m conntrack --ctstate ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT; iptables -P FORWARD DROP`
priya: Linkcheck failing on older internal link /internal/docs/onprem -> update to /docs/private/onprem-migration.md. Add changelog header: "Docs: onprem installer v2 migration (PR 4233)" and include ci/docs-smoke-901 in smoke-tests.
docs-bot: Reminder: PR must include a short troubleshooting checklist: udev rule example, SELinux chcon tip, and systemd BindPaths example.
jamal: udev rule example I use: `KERNEL=="pkcs11", MODE="0660", GROUP="hsm"` and systemd snippet: `BindPaths=/dev/eph-pkcs11:/dev/pkcs11`
security: small note: add a sentence about HSM vendor lib paths varying widely; include sample paths for SoftHSM (`/usr/lib/softhsm/libsofthsm2.so`), SafeNet (`/opt/safenet/lib/libecryptoki.so`), and Cloud vendor shim.
tori: Pushing updates: changelog, linkfix, tiny Go snippet, kms-proxy example, udev+systemd tips, nftables+iptables examples. Tagging @priya for final quick pass. docs-bot: Will re-run linkcheck + smoke-tests on push (ci/docs-smoke-901).
